xe: enable experimental 16k build

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
Upstream-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Base revision: linux-aurora source 6f63677751854d57bcfac172314957bc2197c05f
Status: experimental. Never run on hardware. Not submitted upstream.

License state of the file this patch modifies, as read from its header at the
base revision (keep that header in place; this patch does not add a copyright
line and does not change the SPDX identifier):

  drivers/gpu/drm/xe/Kconfig   GPL-2.0-only

The full GPL-2.0 text ships with the kernel sources it applies to, and is
published at https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/licenses.html

What this patch changes: the Xe driver Kconfig gate also accepts 16K host
pages, so the driver can be selected on the 16K arm64 kernel these hosts use.
Selecting it still requires parts 1, 2 and 4 of this series: this is the build
gate only, and it asserts nothing about runtime correctness. This is part 3 of
4 in the 16K xe series.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/Kconfig
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 	depends on KUNIT || !KUNIT
 	depends on INTEL_VSEC || !INTEL_VSEC
 	depends on X86_PLATFORM_DEVICES || !(X86 && ACPI)
-	depends on PAGE_SIZE_4KB || COMPILE_TEST || BROKEN
+	depends on PAGE_SIZE_4KB || PAGE_SIZE_16KB || COMPILE_TEST || BROKEN
 	select INTERVAL_TREE
 	# we need shmfs for the swappable backing store, and in particular
 	# the shmem_readpage() which depends upon tmpfs
